# Architecture

## Component diagram

\`\`\`mermaid
flowchart TD
  web["Next.js web app"]
  api["API server"]
  db["PostgreSQL"]
  web -->|HTTPS| api
  api -->|reads/writes| db
\`\`\`

## Sequence diagrams — the riskiest flows

### Create a habit

_Why this flow: Creating a habit has the most failure paths and touches every component. (failure paths: 2, touches 3 components)._

\`\`\`mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant User
  participant System
  participant Database
  User->>System: fills in the habit form
  System->>Database: validates the input
  Database->>Database: stores the new habit
  Note over User: Failure — empty name → asks for a name
  Note over User: Failure — database is down → try again shortly
\`\`\`

### Check in on a habit

_Why this flow: Check-in is the highest-frequency flow, so its one failure path matters daily. (failure paths: 1, touches 2 components)._

\`\`\`mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant User
  participant Database
  User->>Database: taps check in
  Database->>Database: records today’s completion
  Note over User: Failure — already checked in today → already done today
\`\`\`
"
